<section id="data">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <p class="ve-label">System of record</p>
    <h2>Google stays the source of truth. The bot is the entrance.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="ve-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Systems of record comparison. Scroll horizontally to explore.">
    <p class="scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">Swipe horizontally to compare →</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>System of record</th><th>Write policy</th><th>Safety detail</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Calendar</th><td>Google Calendar SHUM</td><td>Create, update, delete, restore</td><td>Preview, duplicate detection, JSON-LD poster parsing, external guests through a service account with a 403 fallback.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>HR</th><td>HR workbook, ten profile sheets</td><td>One primary sheet per person</td><td>Candidate deduplication, PDF continuation, human-only <code>Comment</code>, one-click save state machine.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Client Base</th><td>Five active client sheets</td><td>Append or update one row</td><td>Website and domain deduplication, media and PDF input, durable post-save comment.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Budget</th><td>Finance workbook, 3 active sheets</td><td>Expenses, income, expected receipts</td><td>8%&nbsp;AUSN tax, safe arithmetic formulas, raw-cell reads, no-replay save.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>PR and Marketing</th><td>PR workbook</td><td>Append or update in place</td><td>URL deduplication, text-only HTML cards, SSRF-safe enrichment, edit-in-place.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Personal Data</th><td>Dedicated personal-data workbook</td><td>Read-only</td><td>Never sent to AI, never persisted, never logged. One-tap copy cards.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Website Enquiries</th><td>Telegram topic plus admin receipts</td><td>Ingress and anonymize</td><td>Protected endpoint, minimized receipt, no-replay protocol, 30-day anonymization.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="split" style="margin-top:28px">
    <div>
      <p>This is why the admin panel is not a spreadsheet editor. It shows the state of the machine around the data: health, access, events, failures, and cost. The rows themselves stay in Google Sheets, where the team already works and where the formulas and sharing rules already live.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="note-box">
      <h3>The product boundary</h3>
      <p>Google Sheets is the system of record. PostgreSQL is the system of memory: drafts, tokens, locks, incidents, usage, and audit. The two have different jobs and are never allowed to silently become each other.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
